This directory contains two subdirectories: atangle and aweave,
which contains the ada code for same.

It also contains the files:

awebmac.tex:	The TeX macro
		file needed for processing the output of the aweave processor
		into beautiful documentation.

awebman.tex:    The aweb documentation in TeX format.

awebman.ps:	The aweb documentation in PostScript format.


Release 2.2 (Ada 2012)
----------------------

Both atangle and aweave have been upgraded to recognise programs written
in Ada 2012 (ISO/IEC 8652:2012) in addition to Ada 83 and Ada 95.  Four
reserved words have been added to aweave's lexical table so that they
are pretty-printed as keywords rather than as ordinary identifiers:

    interface, overriding, synchronized   (added in Ada 2005)
    some                                  (added in Ada 2012)

The lexical structure of Ada 2012 is unchanged from Ada 95 with respect
to identifiers, so atangle requires no syntactic change; the new
keywords are passed through verbatim and pretty-printed by aweave.

Both programs print their version banner with the -v / --version flag:

    $ atangle --version
    This is ATANGLE, Version 2.2 (Ada 2012)

    $ aweave --version
    This is AWEAVE, Version 2.2 (Ada 2012 keyword support)


Building locally
----------------

To build the aweb programs with GNAT, cd to the respective directory
and type "gnatmake aweave" or "gnatmake atangle".


Running in Docker
-----------------

A Docker image carrying the toolchain is available; the helper script
aweb.sh will build it on first invocation and dispatch atangle/aweave
inside the container:

    ./aweb.sh atangle file.aweb [changefile]
    ./aweb.sh aweave  file.aweb [changefile]
    ./aweb.sh shell                       # interactive shell
    ./aweb.sh test                        # run the STP harness
    ./aweb.sh build                       # rebuild the image

The image is tagged evansjr/aweb:2.2.

